      "title": "Graphing a Curve Defined Parametrically"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "095ebc5b-46a8-50db-a8e2-9f225774c777",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=t \\left(t - 2\\right) - t \\left(t^{2} - 4\\right)\\\\ y&=- t \\left(t + 2\\right) + t \\left(t^{2} - 4\\right) - 2\\\\ &-2\\leq t\\leq 2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First calculate the $x$-values using $x=t \\left(t - 2\\right) - t \\left(t^{2} - 4\\right)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & -2 & -1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ \\hline x & 8 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ \\hline y &  &  &  &  &  \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nNow calculate $y=- t \\left(t + 2\\right) + t \\left(t^{2} - 4\\right) - 2$ at the **same parameter values**:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & -2 & -1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ \\hline x & 8 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ \\hline y & -2 & 2 & -2 & -8 & -10 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nThe successive paired points are $(8,-2)$, $(0,2)$, $(0,-2)$, $(2,-8)$, $(0,-10)$. Use the endpoint pair to find the matching group, then compare an interior paired point to distinguish the remaining curves.\n\n![Curve through the calculated points](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/edb-math/audits/2026-10-30-parametric-plot-readability/current-assets/44f0b1b5e17a6ab6ed122c031f2baa6e4ce2dfba23b93535160f2c4ed1e27764/solution-0.png)",
